  "question": {
    "text": "The sum and product of the mean and variance of a binomial distribution are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>82</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1350</mn></math>&nbsp;respectively. They the number of trials in the binomial distribution is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "96",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Given, sum of mean and variance is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>82</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>Product of roots is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1350</mn></math></p><p>Now, Mean and variance are the roots of&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mfenced><mtext>sum&#160;of&#160;roots</mtext></mfenced><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mtext>product&#160;of&#160;roots</mtext><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>82</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1350</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mtext>or</mtext><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p>So, mean <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>60</mn></math>&nbsp;and variance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi>n</mi><mi>p</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>22</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn></mrow><mn>60</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>So, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>60</mn><mfrac><mn>5</mn><mn>8</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>96</mn></math></p></blockquote>",
